格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"PerryLink DSH plugin family: 96 mainline specs (88 active, 8 frozen) + 24 opt-in domain specs; roster 99 repos. Non-official; no certification.","id":"gh:1335789338","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-kit","slug":"PerryLink/dsh-kit","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","installer","starter-kit"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"PerryLink DSH plugin family: 96 mainline specs (88 active, 8 frozen) + 24 opt-in domain specs; roste"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"r 99 repos. Non-official; no certification."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-kit"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**One-command starter pack for the actively maintained PerryLink DeepSeek Harness plugins, plus froz"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"en ones kept installable.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"dsh-kit is the installer and mainline roster of PerryLink's full DSH plugin family — three-level sta"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ndards and checks, guides, the developer toolchain, runtime plugins, the 53-checker compliance suite"},{"id":"p4s3","text":", domain operations, catalogs, and the separate Phocinae decision line. Each plugin ships with a com"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"plete `dsh.bundle` manifest, five-language docs, CI, and npm publishing."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"*Workflow overview: call → plugin → result. The kit is the maintenance surface.*"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Pick a profile (e.g. `web`), then install everything:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Or install individual plugins:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## What's inside (curated highlights — the installers cover 43 npm specs, plus 53 opt-in (96 total))"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Two of the highlights below are **retired** and one is **frozen**. They all stay listed, and stay\nin"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"stallable, because people already run them: 🧊 **FROZEN** means no new features and only a real break"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"age gets fixed, 🚫 **RETIRED**\nmeans the host now does this natively and the package is npm-deprecate"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"d — retired packages are **not** in\n`plugins.txt`, so a fresh install never pulls them in."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### The Claude Code parity trio"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Plugin | One-liner |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| dsh-checkpoint-rewind | Git-first snapshots before every mutation, session forks, one-shot `/rewin"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"d` restore |\n| dsh-permission-rules | Declarative allow/deny/ask permission rules with audit, dry-ru"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"n and hot reload |\n| dsh-output-styles | Runtime-switchable model output styles with per-session per"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"reload |\n| dsh-output-styles | Runtime-switchable model output styles with per-session persistence |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Memory, agents & workflow"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Plugin | One-liner | Status |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| dsh-memento | Approval-gated cross-session memory: `ctx.memory` + SQLite + `memory` tool | |\n| dsh"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"-background-agents | Durable background child agents: sidebar progress, messaging, interrupt | 🚫 **R"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ETIRED** — the host ships native continuable subagents |\n| dsh-doublecheck | Engineering-discipline "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"guard: requirements grill, test gates, adversary review | |\n| dsh-auto-review | Second-model auto-re"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"view on the approval chain, fail-closed | |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Developer & safety tools"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Plugin | One-liner |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| dsh-mcp-panel | Read-only MCP runtime panel: `/mcp` + Settings tab |\n| dsh-lsp-actions | LSP diagn"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ostics, formatting, completion, code actions, rename |\n| dsh-github-bot | GitHub PR/issue integratio"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"n; every write gated by human approval |\n| dsh-security-pack | Security-audit skill pack: secret sca"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"n, dependency and supply-chain review |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### UX & migration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Plugin | One-liner | Status |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| dsh-session-pin | Pin sessions in the Web sidebar with durable ordering | 🚫 **RETIRED** — the host"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" ships session pinning natively |\n| dsh-composer-history | Terminal-style input history for the web "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"composer: arrows, Ctrl+R | |\n| dsh-primer | Plugin-development knowledge base as an on-demand agent "},{"id":"p24s4","text":"skill | |\n| dsh-claude-move | Migrate Claude Code sessions, memory, skills and CLAUDE.md into DSH | "},{"id":"p24s5","text":"🧊 FROZEN — see the repo README |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Notes"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- The installed set is `plugins.txt` — one npm spec per line, and the only place the roster is writt"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"en down. Both installers read it, and `node scripts/check-parity.mjs` holds them and every count on "},{"id":"p26s3","text":"this page to it.\n- **Retired packages are not in `plugins.txt`**, so a fresh install never pulls one"},{"id":"p26s4","text":" in, and the gate fails if one is added back. The five retired names, and why, are listed in the fil"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"e's own header comment.\n- **Frozen packages are in `plugins.txt`** and are installed; a trailing `# "},{"id":"p26s6","text":"🧊 FROZEN` comment on their line marks them, and both installers strip that comment before calling `d"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"sh plugin add`.\n- Install scripts are **idempotent** — safe to re-run.\n- `dsh-security-pack` install"},{"id":"p26s8","text":"s from npm.\n- Versions track the latest npm releases; pin a specific version per plugin if you need "},{"id":"p26s9","text":"reproducibility.\n- **Monthly download baseline:** `node scripts/npm-downloads-snapshot.mjs` reads th"},{"id":"p26s10","text":"is file's own roster and appends every spec's week and month npm downloads to `data/npm-downloads-sn"},{"id":"p26s11","text":"apshots.json`, so a distribution change can be measured against a previous month instead of asserted"},{"id":"p26s12","text":". It writes only that series — the profile page's download figure stays where it is. See `scripts/RE"},{"id":"p26s13","text":"ADME-npm-downloads-snapshot.md`.\n- Deprecated names are not installed: `dsh-background-agents`, `dsh"},{"id":"p26s14","text":"-session-pin` and `dsh-team-rooms` (the host implements all three natively now), and `dsh-plugin-upg"},{"id":"p26s15","text":"rade-015` plus its earlier name `dsh-plugin-upgrade-rc1` (superseded by `dsh-codemod`, which carries"},{"id":"p26s16","text":" every corridor in one package). They stay on npm for anyone who already installed them.\n- License: "},{"id":"p26s17","text":"Apache-2.0 (matching the plugin family)."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Feedback"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Issues and feature requests: open them on the individual plugin repo, or discuss the whole family on"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" the official DeepSeek Harness Discussions (category \"Show Your Plugins!\")."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## PerryLink DSH Plugin Family"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"This project is part of the DeepSeek Harness plugin family from PerryLink. The family has three laye"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"rs — standards/guides, developer toolchain, runtime/domain plugins — plus the Phocinae decision line"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"; the full group-by-group index is FAMILY.md. The install roster stays collapsed below so every READ"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"ME keeps a short first screen; expand it to see every row and its status."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Expand all plugins"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| Plugin | Status |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| **dsh-aqua-input-check** |  |\n| **dsh-archive-check** |  |\n| **dsh-auto-review** |  |\n| **dsh-auto"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"tier** | 🧊 FROZEN — see the repo README |\n| 